result:
### Rationale
The cluster-of-2 launch is the only change that helps. It cuts about 0.15–0.2 µs per launch at every size with a grid of 1184 CTAs or fewer. The other changes made no measurable difference: 32-bit index math, constant cache policies, a branch-free tail (V1) and 8 floats per thread (V4). Removing the cache hints (V3) hurt at 2.1M and above. A plain launch with the same even-padded grid matched r0, so the cluster launch itself is the cause. run_tests passed 16/16 and put S at -4.9% and M at -4.3%.

